9.1 Recent
9.1.1 Plans for improvement - Recent improvements National classification on kinds of economic activities, Rev.2 has been introduced into national
 statistical practice;
 a tourism satellite account has been introduced into practice;
 in accordance with the recommendations of the SNA 2008, the practice of valuing housing
 services produced by owner-occupiers for their own consumption has been introduced;
 the practice of estimating financial intermediation services indirectly measured (FISIM) and allocating
 them by user industry has been improved;
 data on export and import operations have been brought into conformity with BPM6
 requirements;
 the practice of estimating the non-observed economy has been introduced and its methodological
 basis improved;
 the use of tax and other administrative data in GDP compilation has been expanded;
 the institutional coverage of the general government sector has been expanded;
 the data coverage of output and gross value added calculations by economic activity has been improved;
 work has been carried out to reconcile annual and quarterly GDP estimates and revise the time
 series. 9.2 General
